} :question/id #uuid "3f1782d4-ceb0-5897-9f90-478b4c1242ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-118692" :question/problem "![](images/55/5548481ccbe3aee88fd4b346ad53777b7101223c19f7e8408c8ef85bb0d9df25.png)\n\nGiven the right triangle $△PQR$ shown above, which of the following diagrams represents the height corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PR}?$" :question/worked-solution "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PR}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $Q$ to the line $\\overset{⟷}{PR},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{PR}.$\n\nThe correct diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/30/301c31fa98ce5c016337f422566b94a742e3da126b76f9060e4b13d6a8e86358.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a916099-a237-5612-b7f1-3679b7ff069d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37f6e98b-9e74-5362-9415-76b0e5788bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{26}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251016} {:answer/id #uuid "412b51d2-1c6c-5e96-b7f4-3a46ab2a6b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251093} {:answer/id #uuid "5df0c213-f26e-5d44-b086-a8082f8ff356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{22}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251329} {:answer/id #uuid "6a726442-67f6-5b29-aa0d-827d6fcd828e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{18}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251427} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d0d4d2-0d27-5b44-a286-f8c17048fc8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "412b51d2-1c6c-5e96-b7f4-3a46ab2a6b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251093} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd987d2b-51a1-5e48-9b29-2cadc9f301dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "574c517e-3266-5464-9df0-9e740c923895" :question/math-academy-id "q-118757" :question/problem "![](images/95/95b534f8c159b37884e32b730d9aa502565ff4971cd7d08903ffbfaa94b76623.png)\n\nConsider $△PQR$ shown above. The line segment $\\overset{―}{RH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overset{―}{PQ}.$ If $m∠PQR={118}^{∘},$ calculate $m∠QRH.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HQR+m∠PQR & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HQR+{118}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HQR & ={62}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△QHR$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QRH+m∠HQR+m∠RHQ & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠QRH+{62}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠QRH+{152}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠QRH & ={28}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d27b85e4-ddae-5b5f-965a-5dff51b8449b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Vertex of a Vertical Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "270439e3-e2ab-5a45-87bf-95f9becc4e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250889} {:answer/id #uuid "463b87ff-48d0-5886-a575-321db25afa2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251134} {:answer/id #uuid "68421f23-fdb5-513b-aad2-454ec11b2707" 